At a markedly more accessible price point, the &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj; will likely be the go-to iPhone for many customers, particularly those buying on a budget. Like its predecessor, it makes relatively few compromises compared to the standard model and still delivers most of the features that matter for everyday use. In fact, the &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj; now offers noticeably better performance than the &zwnj;iPhone 16&zwnj; thanks to its newer A19 chip, as well as strong battery life aided by Apple's efficient C1X modem.<br/>
<br/>
For many customers, the absence of an Ultra Wide camera, Camera Control, additional color options, and newer connectivity technologies such as Wi-Fi 7, Thread, and Ultra Wideband may not matter. The &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj; also starts with more storage and costs &#36;100 less than the &zwnj;iPhone 16&zwnj;, making it a compelling option for buyers who primarily care about performance, battery life, and overall value.<br/>
<br/>
However, the &zwnj;iPhone 16&zwnj; still offers several advantages. Features like the &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj;, a brighter display with higher peak brightness outdoors, an Ultra Wide camera with macro photography, Spatial photo and video capture, and a wider range of video features give it a significantly more capable camera system. Additional hardware such as the Ultra Wideband chip, Thread connectivity, mmWave 5G, and Wi-Fi 7 may also be important for users who want the most complete feature set.<br/>
<br/>
